   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# P2-C: Mistral 7B QLoRA — RPG NPC Brain\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal**: Fine-tune Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3 on 247 curated NPC dialogue samples using QLoRA (NF4 base + bf16 LoRA), passing both quality gates:\n",
    "- `in_character` ≥ 4.0\n",
    "- `jailbreak` ≥ 4.0\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hardware**: T4 (16GB) on Colab Free Tier  \n",
    "**Framework**: Unsloth + TRL SFTTrainer  \n",
    "**Estimated time**: ~15–25 min training + ~5 min eval generation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key difference from Mac experiments\n",
    "- Mac used MLX 4-bit (full inference quantized → control token leakage on jailbreak)\n",
    "- This uses NF4 base + **bf16 LoRA adapters** + proper HF system role support → no merging workaround"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install dependencies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%capture\n",
    "# Unsloth: fast QLoRA training (2x speedup over vanilla HF)\n",
    "!pip install unsloth\n",
    "!pip install --upgrade trl datasets transformers accelerate bitsandbytes peft\n",
    "# Restart runtime if prompted"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Mount Google Drive (for saving adapter weights)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "SAVE_DIR = '/content/drive/MyDrive/slm_npc/p2c_mistral7b'\n",
    "os.makedirs(SAVE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(f'Adapter output: {SAVE_DIR}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Upload dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Upload `train.jsonl` and `valid.jsonl` from `data/mlx_curated_medium/` on your local machine."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "print('Upload train.jsonl and valid.jsonl from data/mlx_curated_medium/')\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()  # select both files\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "for fname in uploaded:\n",
    "    print(f'  uploaded: {fname} ({len(uploaded[fname])} bytes)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Load model (NF4 quantized base + bf16 LoRA)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from unsloth import FastLanguageModel\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX_SEQ_LENGTH = 1024\n",
    "\n",
    "model, tokenizer = FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_name='mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3',\n",
    "    max_seq_length=MAX_SEQ_LENGTH,\n",
    "    dtype=None,           # auto-detect (bf16 on A100/T4)\n",
    "    load_in_4bit=True,    # NF4 quantization: ~8GB VRAM for 7B\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Model loaded. VRAM used: {torch.cuda.memory_allocated()/1e9:.2f} GB')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Attach LoRA adapter"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = FastLanguageModel.get_peft_model(\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "    r=8,                          # rank (higher than Qwen 1.5B: more capacity)\n",
    "    target_modules=[\n",
    "        'q_proj', 'k_proj', 'v_proj', 'o_proj',\n",
    "        'gate_proj', 'up_proj', 'down_proj'\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    lora_alpha=16,\n",
    "    lora_dropout=0.05,\n",
    "    bias='none',\n",
    "    use_gradient_checkpointing='unsloth',  # saves VRAM\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model.print_trainable_parameters()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Prepare dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from datasets import Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_jsonl(path):\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    with open(path) as f:\n",
    "        for line in f:\n",
    "            line = line.strip()\n",
    "            if line:\n",
    "                rows.append(json.loads(line))\n",
    "    return rows\n",
    "\n",
    "def format_sample(sample):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Apply Mistral chat template. HF tokenizer handles system role natively.\"\"\"\n",
    "    messages = sample['messages']\n",
    "    text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n",
    "        messages,\n",
    "        tokenize=False,\n",
    "        add_generation_prompt=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return {'text': text}\n",
    "\n",
    "train_raw = load_jsonl('train.jsonl')\n",
    "valid_raw = load_jsonl('valid.jsonl')\n",
    "\n",
    "train_ds = Dataset.from_list(train_raw).map(format_sample)\n",
    "valid_ds = Dataset.from_list(valid_raw).map(format_sample)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Train: {len(train_ds)} samples')\n",
    "print(f'Valid: {len(valid_ds)} samples')\n",
    "print('\\nSample (first 300 chars):')\n",
    "print(train_ds[0]['text'][:300])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Train"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from trl import SFTTrainer\n",
    "from transformers import TrainingArguments\n",
    "from unsloth import is_bfloat16_supported\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer = SFTTrainer(\n",
    "    model=model,\n",
    "    tokenizer=tokenizer,\n",
    "    train_dataset=train_ds,\n",
    "    eval_dataset=valid_ds,\n",
    "    dataset_text_field='text',\n",
    "    max_seq_length=MAX_SEQ_LENGTH,\n",
    "    dataset_num_proc=2,\n",
    "    args=TrainingArguments(\n",
    "        per_device_train_batch_size=4,\n",
    "        gradient_accumulation_steps=1,\n",
    "        warmup_steps=5,\n",
    "        max_steps=150,              # ~150 iters; eval at 25/50/75/100 steps\n",
    "        learning_rate=2e-4,\n",
    "        fp16=not is_bfloat16_supported(),\n",
    "        bf16=is_bfloat16_supported(),\n",
    "        logging_steps=10,\n",
    "        evaluation_strategy='steps',\n",
    "        eval_steps=25,\n",
    "        save_strategy='steps',\n",
    "        save_steps=25,\n",
    "        output_dir=SAVE_DIR,\n",
    "        optim='adamw_8bit',         # 8-bit Adam: saves VRAM\n",
    "        seed=42,\n",
    "        load_best_model_at_end=True,\n",
    "        metric_for_best_model='eval_loss',\n",
    "    ),\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Starting training...')\n",
    "trainer_stats = trainer.train()\n",
    "print(f'\\nDone. Runtime: {trainer_stats.metrics[\"train_runtime\"]:.1f}s')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Save best adapter to Drive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save the best checkpoint adapter weights\n",
    "best_dir = os.path.join(SAVE_DIR, 'best_adapter')\n",
    "model.save_pretrained(best_dir)\n",
    "tokenizer.save_pretrained(best_dir)\n",
    "print(f'Saved to {best_dir}')\n",
    "!ls -lh {best_dir}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Generate eval responses (30 traps)\n",
